WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.335 --> 00:00:04.881
(orchestral music)

00:00:09.177 --> 00:00:11.388
- This is what I hope to see when I die.

00:00:11.388 --> 00:00:13.264
- I mean, I don't know who
doesn't love fried chicken.

00:00:13.264 --> 00:00:15.642
- If you wanna seduce me,
just offer me fried chicken.

00:00:15.642 --> 00:00:17.542
And I'm (snaps) like that.

00:00:17.542 --> 00:00:21.884
(orchestral music)

00:00:22.854 --> 00:00:25.235
- Everyone's gonna win today
because it's fried chicken.

00:00:25.235 --> 00:00:29.258
- Except like your cholesterol
levels and your arteries.

00:00:30.888 --> 00:00:32.451
- This tastes like some off brand chicken.

00:00:32.451 --> 00:00:33.326
- It's good.

00:00:33.326 --> 00:00:34.071
- It's buttery.

00:00:34.071 --> 00:00:34.787
- It's good.

00:00:34.787 --> 00:00:36.121
- This one necessarily
doesn't have that much

00:00:36.121 --> 00:00:37.374
of a crunch to it.

00:00:37.374 --> 00:00:38.749
- It's dark meat, it's fatty, it's rich,

00:00:38.749 --> 00:00:39.916
it's luxurious.

00:00:39.916 --> 00:00:41.627
- That was pretty good,
I'd give it like an eight

00:00:41.627 --> 00:00:42.336
out of 10.

00:00:42.336 --> 00:00:43.754
- I like really, really crispy chicken,

00:00:43.754 --> 00:00:45.539
so I'd give it a five.

00:00:47.257 --> 00:00:48.341
- Oh this smells good.

00:00:48.341 --> 00:00:49.626
- Like the outside isn't really that oily,

00:00:49.626 --> 00:00:53.388
but once you go inside,
it's like a vat of oil.

00:00:53.388 --> 00:00:55.391
- The chicken is a
little dry for my taste.

00:00:55.391 --> 00:00:57.223
- Oh, it's so spicy.

00:00:57.223 --> 00:00:58.852
- It feels like the skin
and the chicken are two

00:00:58.852 --> 00:01:00.511
different things, and I don't like that.

00:01:00.511 --> 00:01:01.104
- I feel like this is--

00:01:01.104 --> 00:01:02.522
- I think it might be Popeyes.

00:01:02.522 --> 00:01:05.441
It's got that nice little Popeyes flavor.

00:01:05.441 --> 00:01:08.008
- Five out of ten, would not eat again

00:01:08.008 --> 00:01:10.083
if these weren't in front of me.

00:01:11.073 --> 00:01:13.192
- Already 100% sure this is KFC.

00:01:13.192 --> 00:01:14.326
- You know your chicken.

00:01:14.326 --> 00:01:17.203
- Oh, I just got a huge bite of grease.

00:01:17.203 --> 00:01:19.664
- This one made my spit
really stick to the chicken

00:01:19.664 --> 00:01:20.915
as I pulled away from it.

00:01:20.915 --> 00:01:22.166
- I dig this one.

00:01:22.166 --> 00:01:23.836
This is probably first
place for me right now.

00:01:23.836 --> 00:01:25.003
- I don't know, this is pretty good,

00:01:25.003 --> 00:01:27.320
but I don't think it's as
good as Roscoe's or Louisiana.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:28.047
- No.

00:01:28.047 --> 00:01:30.550
- This tastes to me like
the most processed so far.

00:01:30.550 --> 00:01:32.432
- It's mostly breading.

00:01:32.432 --> 00:01:33.839
- You know what, I'm just
gonna take another bite

00:01:33.839 --> 00:01:36.558
because I might not eat dinner tonight.

00:01:38.368 --> 00:01:40.094
- (muffled speaking)

00:01:40.094 --> 00:01:41.144
- Did you say "take me to church?"

00:01:41.144 --> 00:01:42.563
- I like this one.

00:01:42.563 --> 00:01:43.805
- This one is very, very greasy.

00:01:43.805 --> 00:01:46.023
This came like straight from the fire.

00:01:46.023 --> 00:01:48.112
- I hope I don't get diarrhea. (laughs)

00:01:48.112 --> 00:01:49.685
- This is definitely the
best wing I've had so far.

00:01:49.685 --> 00:01:50.612
- It's too wet.

00:01:50.612 --> 00:01:51.696
- Yeah, it's really wet.

00:01:51.696 --> 00:01:53.068
I don't like it.

00:01:53.068 --> 00:01:55.074
- I don't know what this
brand is, but I'm not...

00:01:55.074 --> 00:01:56.992
Maybe this was the church one.

00:01:56.992 --> 00:01:57.654
- That's too much...

00:01:57.654 --> 00:01:59.955
It's not even chicken
anymore, it's just fried skin.

00:01:59.955 --> 00:02:01.956
You have some skin on your lip.

00:02:01.956 --> 00:02:03.791
(laughs)

00:02:04.793 --> 00:02:07.162
- Smell that.

00:02:07.162 --> 00:02:08.248
- (exhales excitedly)

00:02:08.248 --> 00:02:09.130
- I like the skin.

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:09.789
- Mhm.

00:02:09.789 --> 00:02:12.008
- Mm, that flavor, damn!

00:02:12.008 --> 00:02:13.594
- This one was like the perfect dessert

00:02:13.594 --> 00:02:15.053
to the rest of these.

00:02:15.053 --> 00:02:16.596
- Look at how much chicken as well.

00:02:16.596 --> 00:02:18.973
Like this came from an
animal, you can tell.

00:02:18.973 --> 00:02:20.896
- This one is seasoned
really, really well.

00:02:20.896 --> 00:02:23.640
(muffled speaking)

00:02:24.390 --> 00:02:25.814
- Winner winner, chicken dinner.

00:02:25.814 --> 00:02:26.564
Boom!

00:02:26.564 --> 00:02:27.356
- Boom!

00:02:27.356 --> 00:02:28.892
- That one.

00:02:30.772 --> 00:02:35.199
- Louisiana, Popeyes, KFC,

00:02:35.199 --> 00:02:38.534
Church's, Roscoe's.

00:02:39.578 --> 00:02:43.832
- Roscoe's, Popeyes, KFC, Church's,

00:02:43.832 --> 00:02:45.835
Louisiana.

00:02:46.544 --> 00:02:50.386
(screaming excitedly)

00:02:52.006 --> 00:02:53.175
- [Both] We got it right!?

00:02:53.175 --> 00:02:55.450
- We got it all right?

00:02:55.450 --> 00:02:57.178
- [Both] Yeah!

00:02:57.178 --> 00:02:59.139
- Boys, we're boys!

00:02:59.139 --> 00:03:00.724
We're boys who like chicken!

00:03:00.724 --> 00:03:02.310
Boys, we're boys,

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.836
who like (bleep) fried chicken!

00:03:04.836 --> 00:03:07.438
Pick the chicken up, take a big bite,

00:03:07.438 --> 00:03:11.276
let it down to the floor,
and have a good night, woo!

